cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you build on this software, findings, or ideas, please cite this repository and the exact commit used."
type: software
title: "RALUP: Representation-aware learned update policy"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.1.0
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/adaptive-calculus"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/adaptive-calculus"
abstract: >-
  Exploratory research on learned update selection for a byte Transformer with
  simulated E2M1 FP4 forward weights and FP32 shadows, arithmetic and optimizer
  state. Backpropagation supplies gradients. Two provisional one-step ES policies
  from the same proxy META task improved short endpoints but worsened the
  remaining 496-step endpoint by +0.006914 and +0.013553 bits per byte relative
  to the initialized policy. These diagnostics establish no scientific advantage;
  matched finalist comparisons and protected-test confirmation remain unresolved.
keywords:
  - learned optimizers
  - quantization
  - E2M1
  - byte language models
  - research infrastructure
  - inconclusive results
